{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/603273-changeling-involvement-with-garou-that-makes-sense","id":603273,"title":"Changeling - involvement with Garou that makes sense","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-07-25T16:23:53-07:00","id":603273,"title":"Changeling - involvement with Garou that makes sense","content":"In the Werewolf forum long ago, I asked about ways to properly involve Changelings with Garou since my players are in a pack with Stag, and its ban is to always help faeries in need. Werewolf doesn't give many ideas on how to make that ban important, and I got a few ideas out of it.<br /> <br /> Now I'd like to hear from Changelings ST and players about the reverse situation. Assuming a typical Changeling court in the region, how and why would they involve Garou. I'm hoping to hear lots of different ideas here. It could be fae making Garou enchanted and then abusing them as slave bodyguards to truly being good allies who reciprocally help the pack and call for their aide.<br /> <br /> Assuming there is no existing tie between them (kinfolk are also kinain for example), how would Changelings become aware of a Garou pack devoted to Stag? How would they approach them? How would they determine they would be safe to interact with? How would Unseelie treat them as opposed to Seelie? If you were Changeling PCs, and the ST made it known their was potentially friendly Garou (a pack is devoted to Stag who is a friend of the Fae), what would you do?<br /> <br /> One of my players is more of a Changeling fan than Werewolf, and while I am not that interested in crossover, I'd like to figure out some kind of situation where we can explore this.<br /> <br /> I ultimately see this Stag Pack of Garou as uneasy allies with the local fae more than anything else, but I'm not quite sure how to get there, or how that could change base on the interaction that happens in game. (I am a big believer in allowing players to change their environment and make fae as their enemies or friends based on their own actions and decisions).<br /> <br /> All ideas welcome. Thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-25T18:57:09-07:00","id":603359,"title":"","content":"That's tricky, because changelings aren't generally keen to check up on werewolves, unless their threshold for gaining Glamour involves fear from Garou rampages (so Unseelie might end up more comfortable with them than Seelie). And, of course, even if there's a favorable mutual interest for both parties... it's generally well-accepted that being around Garou is never safe, strictly speaking. But then, that might also attract less ethically challenged thrillseekers who find that they enjoy the rush of living on the edge whenever the enemies of the werewolves come knocking, and who fight mundanity by throwing themselves into helping the Garou in grand style, which could get old very quickly even for children of Stag as they're obligated to keep the nigh-suicidal changelings from killing themselves trying to take on super-ripped Throwback fomori or nexus crawlers.<br /> <br /> Of course, it might even just be an existing occasional relationship forged from keeping really banal goblin fomori off of the changelings' backs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-25T20:38:55-07:00","id":603436,"title":"","content":"A simple way to do it is the good ol' Damsel in Distress. Just make the Pack cross paths with a Changeling in need for whatever reason. Even common Fomori can threat one of them. From that, most Changelings are prone to look for the PCs again for whatever reason. Some can fall in love almost instantly for one or more of the pack members, others will feel they have to repay the kindness, and yet others will simply think of ways to use the Garou to their own ends.<br /> <br /> Changelings are literally the stuff of dreams and stories. Once you enter the life of one of them, it can be pretty hard to get rid of her. Specially when they find ways to harness Glamour and avoid Banality through this friendship. Some of them will be kindhearted and just want to help. Heck, some of them CAN help, a lot. Others can be as nasty and disgusting as the worse among the servitors of the Wyrm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-25T21:33:10-07:00","id":603478,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/603273-changeling-involvement-with-garou-that-makes-sense?p=603436#post603436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A simple way to do it is the good ol' Damsel in Distress. Just make the Pack cross paths with a Changeling in need for whatever reason.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for your feedback, but I see I need to clarify what I need. I'm not interested in how to make an initial connection between a Changeling/Fae and a Garou, nor personal interaction between them. That is easy to do. I am more interested in how the fae society/local court would interact with Garou who are supposed to be an &quot;ally&quot; of them (whether it is a Fianna, or pack with Stag should be immaterial as both count; in those areas where there aren't Fianna to interact with local fae, the packs of Stag should be filling the same role even if not to the same degree).<br /> <br /> Changeling and Werewolf are supposed to be the most &quot;natural&quot; of crossovers. Werewolves are supposed to have the closest relations of the fae out of all the Prodigals. But what does that mean? Going from vague sentences to real details is a challenge. The Changeling gamebooks that talk about changelings and Garou say things like &quot;Fianna protect visiting sidhe from the Get of Fenris&quot;, Fianna spake as Kithain representatives in negotiations&quot;, &quot;Fianna were dealing with Changeling commoners for centuries&quot;, &quot;Kithain and Garou are often found together&quot;, &quot;Kithain often need stalwart companions for adventure and Garou fit the bill&quot;, &quot;Fianna bards are welcome into fae freeholds&quot;, and &quot;Kithain often in attendance at Garou moots.&quot;<br /> <br /> This is substantial interaction.<br /> <br /> So fae society is often, even if not always, fairly well integrated with the Children of Stag (but probably only them for obvious reasons). This is more than some random Garou running into some random fae. To a certain extent, the Children of Stag are <i>integrated</i> into the local fae/changeling society.<br /> <br /> So how do the local fae do that? There are obvious concerns of the Garou going beserk on occassion, and concern that Garou who are not children of Stag remain dangerous.<br /> <br /> Thanks, I appreciate your response.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-25T21:53:55-07:00","id":603492,"title":"","content":"It &quot;works&quot; by those details being described in Changeling and not Werewolf, much like the supposed vendetta of the Get of Fenris against every kithain that isn't a troll. You're going to have to lean an awful lot more on Changeling to make it work, which means that some Werewolf stuff might get a bit hazy and out of focus. Beyond that, I'd imagine that there would be some kithain who hang around the Garou for the novelty and prestige, some that really aim to build bridges, and some on two sides of &quot;use at all costs/get rid of them&quot; schemes. All in all, it suppose it would be kind of like being the male crew of the Nirvana in Vandread, but with werewolves and romanticized feudalism instead of sex-segregated interstellar societies and space pirates. At least, that's the picture and narrative that came up into my head, and it won't leave.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-26T00:34:21-07:00","id":603591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/603273-changeling-involvement-with-garou-that-makes-sense?p=603492#post603492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> You're going to have to lean an awful lot more on Changeling to make it work, which means that some Werewolf stuff might get a bit hazy and out of focus.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am fine with that which is why I posted this in the general WoD forum instead of the Werewolf forum. I wan the Changeling perspective. I'll adapt as needed to make it work with my chronicle.<br /> <br /> I don't like Crossover games in the sense if PCs being from multiple books. However, I have no problem combining details from the major five game lines for my PCs to interact with as long as I can do so appropriately for the story I want to tell.<br /> <br /> Personally, I depict the fae as similar to the faeries in Mike Mignola's Hellboy. I just have to make tweaks to get the WoD Changelings to get there, I'm just trying to figure out how a Changeling society would integrate &quot;allied&quot; Garou.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-26T02:35:01-07:00","id":603693,"title":"","content":"The changeling approach to Werewolves is that they're scary as hell,attract the worst kind of attention, and are the long lost cousins that you hope don't show up for Thanksgiving. when there IS Changeling / Garou interaction, it usually takes the form of the two groups boning themselves silly, <i>or</i> the Garou getting the bad end of a bargain.<br /> <br /> Or both.<br /> <br /> After all, Changelings are <i>highly</i> political creatures. Them of them as vampires, but without the &quot;sucking wyrm-taint through a straw&quot; feature. If a changeling is risking its neck to be around a psycho death machine, then it inevitably wants something. it could be something as innocuous as some fur clippings (yay, dross!) or maybe it wants you and your pack to be its latest pawns in a literal game of chess on the freehold lawn. Maybe the motley you run into wouldn't mind sending you after their 'corrupt, abusive tyrannical count&quot; - or maybe that count wants to get you on his side to keep the snarling redcaps and rebellious trolls at bay.<br /> <br /> Worst part is, the exploitation is only one way - Changelings are next to useless in the fight for Gaia. Sure, the Nockers can fire up their war machines, the Sidhe can mount their griffins, and it looks awesome until they smack into the &quot;other side&quot; and <i>everything dissolves</i> because the entropic, world-devouring abominations you fight are Changeling kryptonite (both parties learn quickly that your fomori are not <i>their</i> fomori, let's put it)<br /> <br /> for a different approach, consider the nunnehi - they know <i>roughly</i> where the garou are coming from, seeing as how they interact with spirits familiar to the Garou, and they are the last survivors of cultures desperately holding on. Some of them are even fairly decent in a fight (though banality is still a problem). They also work well as antagonists, with stronger &quot;werewolf&quot; themes. Nunnehi benefit from caerns much like werewolves do, and some young (stupid) braves might not be adverse to conducting a raid while your characters are on guard duty. Do you fight them and risk ticking off your totem? Or do you let them slurp some gnosis? They won't <i>hurt</i> the caern, but allowing them to do this will disadvantage your sept's resources, after all... And doing anything in retaliation could not only upset your totem... but some other garou tribes.<br /> <br /> If you're werewolf-centric, then something like a Fianna caern that is near some annoying Nunnehi seems more workable than really trying to dip into the byzantine labyrinth of Kithain society.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/612-the-cat-came-back","name":"The Cat Came Back","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar612_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"243"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-26T07:14:56-07:00","id":603797,"title":"","content":"There are lots of reasons they might have meaningful relationships: defending nature and magical sites, battling Technocrats, joining together to fulfil an oath or quest. <br /> <br /> The major problem with any game featuring both creatures is that the werewolves are largely cut off from chimerical reality. I find that either enchanting Garou or having them swear an oath to the fae or Dreaming (e.g., to defend a magical site which is both a caern and a rath to a freehold) is necessary to allow them to see the world as changelings do. <br /> <br /> Once that's done, however, things become much easier. Werewolves and fae can bind themselves to each other, and as both are creatures of honour (usually), that gives them reasons to interact. From there, all kinds of interesting things could happen: fae in the Umbra, Garou in the Dreaming, all manner of mythic adventures. <br /> <br /> But without enchantment, changelings just appear like any other mortals, and the wonderful world they live in is invisible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-26T10:48:46-07:00","id":603941,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/603273-changeling-involvement-with-garou-that-makes-sense?p=603797#post603797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">having them swear an oath to the fae or Dreaming</div> </div> </div> </div>This gives me something to think about thanks.<br /> <br /> Please note I am not looking for story or setting ideas. I already have those. Also, I am not running a chronicle where Fae-Garou societies are close. There aren't even Fianna in the game. The <i>only</i> interaction the Garou will have is through this pack of Stag. I just want to make the ban meaningful for the PCs, and there is one PC who would have fun with some level of interaction with the local fae.<br /> <br /> I'm really only looking for ideas and examples of how/why the local Changelings would reach out to a pack of Stag, and then how the local changeling society (not just one or two odd changelings) would treat them and possibly make them part of their society. So the idea of them making oaths and such is a good one.<br /> <br /> In case it matters, here is a short synopsis of the local setting. There is a low level caern basically in a forest preserve outside a major city. This is the &quot;home&quot; caern of the PCs. Of course, there are other caerns in the greater region. Somewhere away from this caern is a major freehold in the wilderness where the local changeling noble lives with his court. There are minor freeholds elsewhere where other changelings survive (in the major city and smaller towns), but they owe fealty to this noble in the major freehold. There are scattered glades and trods out there. Most of these areas are outside the local Garou protectorate, but are accessible. The PCs could run into some random fae/changelings in their normal course, but for the most part, it'll be up to the Changelings to decide to make contact given the reality of the Dreaming and Enchantment.<br /> <br /> I figure any local fae (or at least the important ones) are aware of the pack because of Stag. The local nobles know that any packs that follow Stag have a ban that makes them help any fae when asked. There's all potential for abuse here, but whether the changeling noble is reasonable or abusive doesn't matter. At some point, the fae will reach out to them. How is the local noble going to do that?<br /> <br /> Obviously at some point, Enchantment is required. That's easy. There will be one or more Oaths taken at some point, but remember that by taking Stag as their totem, the pack members have already - essentially - taken a major oath as it is. These are types of things I'm thinking of.<ul><li>Is some kind of official delegation or herald sent to the pack to invite them to the noble court at some point simply because they are children of Stag?</li> <li>Would invitations be sent &quot;early on&quot; in the sense the noble may not need help right now, but he wants to evaluate them early on? Or would they wait until they need some kind of help?</li> <li>As children of Stag, would the fae already accept them as being part of &quot;us&quot; (a lawful part of changeling society) and a natural part of Changeling society, or will the Garou always be &quot;them&quot; (nearby outsiders/barbarians who can be made &quot;friends of Rome&quot; so to speak)?</li> <li>How much authority would the head changeling noble believe he has over this nearby pack of Stag? Would he feel they are natural servants/retainers to be ordered around with Arts like Sovereign if needed? Or would he be more wary because he know Garou can leave packs and even susceptible to frenzy? What is the balance between diplomacy and authority?</li> <li>What kind of arrangements would they make with newly contacted pack of Stag so they could quickly summon them for help if needed?</li> <li>Assuming the PCs are interested and amenable, would they be wanted to regularly attend fae courts and such, and if so under what conditions (oaths, use of Sovereign, etc.)</li> <li>Would other changelings beside the head noble reach out independently? Or is this something that would be left to the local chief? Could packs of Stag be considered the equivalent of knights who are expected to help commoners when they are threatened?</li> </ul>The PCs are still Cliaths right now. However, once they turn Fostern and are &quot;adults&quot;, I'm thinking it would be a good time for the local Changelings to make contact with them.<br /> <br /> \u200bThanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","user":"Black Fox","date":". 07-26-2015, 01:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-26T22:25:03-07:00","id":604500,"title":"","content":"I don't think the Fae are going to know them because of Stag. You see, the same way the Garou are oblivious to the Dreaming, so Changelings are to the Umbra. Tough Stag's Ban does suggest some connetion, the nature of such connection doesn't mean the Fae already know shit about the pack.<br /> <br /> Changelings aren't just political, they are highly ritualistic. You can expect a Sidhe Lord in special to send delegations and stuff, hold court and all. So...<br /> <br /> An official delegation to invite them to court is likely to occur as soon as the lord knows the Garou can be of some use. No matter what he knows of them, he will first prepare in case things go sour, after all, they're raging werewolfs, not pookas, but as soon as he sees it as profitable and get prepared for the meeting, he will send a delegation with all the luxury possible (at least from the Dreaming perspective. They can be quite ragtag on the matherial view, depending on these particular Changelings) and make quite a show for the Garou.<br /> <br /> Fae aren't dumb, and much less eager to thrust. They survived the Autumn, after all. So the first thing any sensible noble will do is to SPY on the pack. As soon as he thinks he can invite them without dooming the meeting instantly, he will do it with all precautions in place. But them, if good for business, he will send messages and call them as early as possible, to stablish good relations ahead of time. Specialy to have an advantage over his rivals. He'll evaluate them and start to buy them to his cause, or at least to his goodwill.<br /> <br /> Garou are the closest among the Prodigals, but still Prodigals. Changeling society does have a place for allies, but never the same of a true Changeling, tough that isn't quite the same as an outsider. It is more like a pet. He can be more of your home than your neighbor, you can thrust him more, but in the end he is just a pet.<br /> <br /> Working with Prodigals a smart noble will allways give precedence to diplomacy, because things can get nasty. But don't be fooled. At heart all nobles believe in their right to command. That doesn't mean they are all assholes, but most are if pressed. They aren't all arrogant, but the great majority are. But even the most kind and humble will use Sovereign if too pressed, even if to apologise after. And Lords rarely are so humble.<br /> <br /> To summon the pack they would probably send messengers, maybe some stationary envoys to take residence nearby the Caern for the Garou to contact quickly and be contacted quicker. Only in some instances would they give any magical communicator, since their magic is also susceptible to Banality.<br /> <br /> Require Prodigals to attend court isn't common, but also not impossible. Only if the lord of the Freehold wants from them some kind of social help will this be likely to happen. Or if he wants them to see how he is good and honorable with his people, to later make an appeal for help against enemies. Some oaths can be required dependent on context, but the simplest level of Sovereign is precisely to assure good behavior during court, so it isn't quite a problem, they will just have to accept this single use of Sovereign on them regularly.<br /> <br /> Since Stag's Ban requires it, the pack will have to behave like knights in shining armor, for sure! But the Changelings aren't dumb, as I said, and will be cautious at first. But as soon as they sense the pack can help, expect them to reach the pack a lot. The noble have enemies, both outside and inside the Freehold. There are probably conspiratorial commoners. Webs of lies and truths intermingled. The Freehold can change from dream to nightmare fast if the pack thinks those fellas are simple, pure stupid or weak. Changeling politics can be as convoluted as the worst the Camarilla have to offer, and the characters are likely to be drag to it if they aren't cautious. The Changelings will reach them and ask for help, against other Changelings that asked also for help, and the pack can end up wishing they had to help vampires.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T19:33:23-07:00","id":610264,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/603273-changeling-involvement-with-garou-that-makes-sense?p=604500#post604500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think the Fae are going to know them because of Stag.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is something I constantly wrestle with as the details of this initial interaction aren't well defined. Here are things I've considered.<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>If a Changeling &quot;prays&quot; to Stag for help, Stag may contact one of his pack children through their pack totem.</li> <li>A Changeling might use one or more of the Soothsay Arts to find/contact a local pack of Stag</li> <li>A Changeling, particular nobles, may possess some kind of Fae Treasure or Artifact that alerts him that a pack of Stag is local to the area. This is something I feel could be quite widespread especially treasures that were created long ago.</li> <li>A Chimerling spirit might enter a Garou's dream and guide them to contact; Chimera in Garou is more a spirit of enigma than part of the Dreaming, but I feel they are at least tenuously connected.</li> </ol><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Changelings aren't just political, they are highly ritualistic. You can expect a Sidhe Lord in special to send delegations and stuff, hold court and all. So... </div> </div> </div>Good point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So the first thing any sensible noble will do is to SPY on the pack. </div> </div> </div>What are some good ways a fae noble could spy on the pack? Ordering a commoner to approach/observe a Garou is possible, but I assume the commoner would be reluctant. Could he send a sentient Chimera to spy? I'm unsure of the rules how a creature in the Near Dreaming could observe the Realm.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> To summon the pack they would probably send messengers, maybe some stationary envoys to take residence nearby the Caern for the Garou to contact quickly and be contacted quicker. </div> </div> </div>What kinf of stationary envoys? Are we talking Chimera again, or something else? Known/allied Kinain? Actual Changelings? In my case, this is hardly likely to be the actual Caern, but a spot protected by the pack is plausible.<br /> <br /> Require Prodigals to attend court isn't common, but also not impossible. Only if the lord of the Freehold wants from them some kind of social help will this be likely to happen. Or if he wants them to see how he is good and honorable with his people, to later make an appeal for help against enemies. Some oaths can be required dependent on context, but the simplest level of Sovereign is precisely to assure good behavior during court, so it isn't quite a problem, they will just have to accept this single use of Sovereign on them regularly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Changelings will reach them and ask for help, against other Changelings that asked also for help, and the pack can end up wishing they had to help vampires. </div> </div> </div>This is something I've also struggled with. Since the Ban is generic, it's hard for one Changeling to ask the pack to fight the other (although any personal oaths would complicate this kind of implied neutrality). It also implies no distinction between the Seelie and Unseelie, although I assume the worst Changelings who could be allied with the Dark or Fomorians or whatever they call it would be treated the same way as any other minion of the Wyrm.<br /> <br /> One thing I'm sure all Changelings would keep aware of is that a Garou who is a member of a pack of Stag isn't bound to be permanently done so. They could quite the pack at any time, and abuse by Changelings of the Totem Ban would be paid in blood. Therefore, I assume most Changelings would avoid bad treatment of their allies - except for the worst bunch who may have sucked personal oaths out of the pack. Then again, the pack likely has friends in their sept who aren't bound by such Bans either. In any case, Changelings are likely on their best behaviour.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T01:28:28-07:00","id":610552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is something I constantly wrestle with as the details of this initial interaction aren't well defined. Here are things I've considered.<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>If a Changeling &quot;prays&quot; to Stag for help, Stag may contact one of his pack children through their pack totem.</li> <li>A Changeling might use one or more of the Soothsay Arts to find/contact a local pack of Stag</li> <li>A Changeling, particular nobles, may possess some kind of Fae Treasure or Artifact that alerts him that a pack of Stag is local to the area. This is something I feel could be quite widespread especially treasures that were created long ago.</li> <li>A Chimerling spirit might enter a Garou's dream and guide them to contact; Chimera in Garou is more a spirit of enigma than part of the Dreaming, but I feel they are at least tenuously connected.</li> </ol></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Just remember to filter this relation through the Changelings perception. They probably don't know of Stag or don't relate to him this way, because they don't deal with Spirits or Umbral denizens of any sort. But for sure they would remember ancient pacts and long standing relationships with Garou that fight under this strange banner.<br /> </span><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">What are some good ways a fae noble could spy on the pack? Ordering a commoner to approach/observe a Garou is possible, but I assume the commoner would be reluctant. Could he send a sentient Chimera to spy? I'm unsure of the rules how a creature in the Near Dreaming could observe the Realm.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Near Dreaming isn't another reality like the Penumbra. Chimeras on it perceive the matherial without any problem at all, they just can't physicaly interact with non-chimerical things. So chimeras can do the job quite well if they don't find any source of Banality. If they do, tough, they will be quite sensible to it, so they will probably avoid. Sending underlings, using Arts and even magical treasures, the Noble will have a lot of alternatives to do so. And in the beginning it is very unlikely that the Garou will be able to perceive or counter such espionage.<br /> <br /> Likewise, tough, don't expect the Fae's resources and spies to be able to deal with the Umbra.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">What kinf of stationary envoys? Are we talking Chimera again, or something else? Known/allied Kinain? Actual Changelings? In my case, this is hardly likely to be the actual Caern, but a spot protected by the pack is plausible.</div> </div> </div> </div>Changelings, in a place near the Caern, but not there, of course.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is something I've also struggled with. Since the Ban is generic, it's hard for one Changeling to ask the pack to fight the other (although any personal oaths would complicate this kind of implied neutrality). It also implies no distinction between the Seelie and Unseelie, although I assume the worst Changelings who could be allied with the Dark or Fomorians or whatever they call it would be treated the same way as any other minion of the Wyrm.</div> </div> </div> </div>You will have to be a lot more strict here. he words on the Ban are quite clear: to never refuse to aid Fae when asked. Even in a common Werewolf game, it isn't your job to define a reasonable interpretation for Bans, but a job for the pack to figure out how to deal with dubious cases. When the Fae get involved, the theme in question is the Oath, and it get very serious. Oaths don't work by the spirit of the law, but by its letter. In fact, your players can outright KILL Changelings if the Fae doesn't ask for help before. If you don't want to place this kind of conundrum, just don't make the Changelings press in those directions. But that's how it works. They literally can't refuse aid to a Fae when asked, be this creature Changeling, Chimera, Dauntain, Fomorian or whatever. And these creatures aren't going to let pass the opportunity when they find this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing I'm sure all Changelings would keep aware of is that a Garou who is a member of a pack of Stag isn't bound to be permanently done so. They could quite the pack at any time, and abuse by Changelings of the Totem Ban would be paid in blood. Therefore, I assume most Changelings would avoid bad treatment of their allies - except for the worst bunch who may have sucked personal oaths out of the pack. Then again, the pack likely has friends in their sept who aren't bound by such Bans either. In any case, Changelings are likely on their best behaviour.</div> </div> </div> </div>Remember that they don't know what is a pack, a totem or a Ban, they only know what they can see. Surely they will be aware of potential problems. But they're also very different from Fera about how they think and how they do business. A lot of them can become a pain in the ass without ever intending so. Sometimes even trying to help. They have their own tricks and can do a lot to defend themselfs if threatened. The Changelings can do a lot even to strip the Garou of allies if hard pressed. Just by being Enchanted the Garou can have a VERY hard time, because the Chimerical reality becomes visible and solidy to them whyle their allies can't even figure out why they are talking with bushes and trees. Imagine an assault of Chimeras on the Caern, but the caern itself isn't in danger. In fact, the only ones in danger are the pack. The other members of the Caern can't even SEE what's harassing the pack.<br /> <br /> Also, Changelings rarely are too reasonable. They are made of Glamour. Living dreams. First, stories and adventure is what makes them tick. Second, most of them are at least a bit crazy. Third, and you have to know this, most Changelings are <b><u>children</u></b>. With all their power and social finesse, a lot of Changelings are between 6 and 12 years old, another bunch go from here to mid-twenties at most. Few Changelings have more than thirty. And fourth, Changelings reincarnate, and they are pretty aware of that. That means they don't fear death as much as mortals and most supernaturals do. To them it is just a short retirement. And them they come back anew, again as children...<br /> <br /> Of course, it doesn't mean the Changelings WILL cause that much trouble. But if you want to stir some, those are your tools. The Garou are powerful, but so are the Fae, in their own way. And they can mess a lot with Werewolfs' expectations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T10:02:22-07:00","id":610989,"title":"","content":"Okay. if you're not &quot;doing crossover&quot; then here's what you need to do...<br /> <br /> Scrap &quot;Changeling.&quot; Write it off, take a pass. Changeling's a fun game, and it's fun in crossover, but if you're just werewolf and looking for &quot;faerie guest-stars&quot; then it's a wash. Changelings are <i>severely</i> under-powered in comparison to the demands of a werewolf game, and the only way to really &quot;get the most&quot; out of them is to basically set werewolf aside and play the Garou in Changeling for a while.<br /> <br /> Werewolf sources pose Fae as hazardous tricksters and semi-elemental spirits, scions of the Wyld who are rapidly fading away from the onslaught of mankind, but who are still not to be trifled with. If you give the pack a 9 year-old kid who insists he's really a six-foot-tall blue dude but he can't show them... it doesn't work well.<br /> <br /> Forget Changeling, and think &quot;Fae&quot;. Powerful, mercurial, semi-spirit beings with strange customs and societies, but yet still 'real&quot; enough to bump into a Stag pack.<br /> <br /> if you need systems for such creatures, go with Dark Ages: Fae. <i>Those</i> things can fit on the same scales as Garou, and definitely have the primal, uncanny nature that the Garou ascribe. Pick out a particular set of myths you want to explore, build some Inanimae or Firstborn to go with those legends, and have the Garou basically deal with the Legendary Realm, without an umbral quest. You're just using Dark Ages: Fae for systems - don't worry too much about the society described or how it &quot;translates&quot; seven hundred years later. Make it up. and make it weird.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/612-the-cat-came-back","name":"The Cat Came Back","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar612_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"243"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T14:49:52-07:00","id":611386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/603273-changeling-involvement-with-garou-that-makes-sense?p=610552#post610552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They probably don't know of Stag or don't relate to him this way, because they don't deal with Spirits or Umbral denizens of any sort. But for sure they would remember ancient pacts and long standing relationships with Garou that fight under this strange banner.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think there is a difference between understanding one thing well (the Dreaming and its chimerical inhabitants, and not knowing anything about how some of the Prodigals operate. It depends on the specific Fae/Changeling. Given the implied interaction, most Fae probably understand there are Garou who know the Dreaming and help the Fae because of ancient Oaths, but that these are a minority and the others showed be avoided. The elder Fae or those with more knowledge probably have a better understanding of the lore involved.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Near Dreaming isn't another reality like the Penumbra. Chimeras on it perceive the matherial without any problem at all, they just can't physicaly interact with non-chimerical things. </div> </div> </div>Understood. Thanks.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You will have to be a lot more strict here. he words on the Ban are quite clear: to never refuse to aid Fae when asked. Even in a common Werewolf game, it isn't your job to define a reasonable interpretation for Bans, but a job for the pack to figure out how to deal with dubious cases. </div> </div> </div>I understand what you mean. But I do think it is part of my job to define the limits of Bans. A big part of the game is seeing how the players react to any given situation. On the other hand, I run all the NPCs. Those NPCs are aware of the thousands of years of actual practice of those Bans and what happens - they get passed down as lore, myth, and history. A Fae/Changeling can certainly ask for forms of help that go beyond what is normal, but there would be precedent of what really fits. And even if the players don't know what is reasonable, their pack Totem does have a better understanding because it is an aspect of Stag.<br /> <br /> The Ban only requires Garou to aide a Fae when asked. Not to be ordered by one. Garou can decide to help the Fae in a way they think fit, and not the way the Fae would like them to do so.<br /> <br /> I think we're actually in agreement here, but we're coming it as from opposite directions. The real question is at what level the GM giving players advice (either through Mentors or Totems or other NPCs, or even OOC to help new players understand the setting), and when to let them figure everything out on their own.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Remember that they don't know what is a pack, a totem or a Ban, they only know what they can see. </div> </div> </div>Again, it depends on the individual Fae/Changeling. Many may be very ignorant. Some are probably very well informed due to Remembrance, lore, Greymayre, Chimerical advisors, whatever.<br /> <br /> Many details may not be known about the Garou world, but that Garou often live in packs like wolves, and that they have gods (Totems) they swear Oaths to is probably fairly basic. A Commoner childling may be ignorant, but a Sidhe noble grump probably does.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Of course, it doesn't mean the Changelings WILL cause that much trouble. But if you want to stir some, those are your tools. The Garou are powerful, but so are the Fae, in their own way. And they can mess a lot with Werewolfs' expectations. </div> </div> </div>Completely agree.<br /> <br /> Thanks for your comments.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T15:00:49-07:00","id":611392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Cat Came Back</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/603273-changeling-involvement-with-garou-that-makes-sense?p=610989#post610989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Scrap &quot;Changeling.&quot; Write it off, take a pass. Changeling's a fun game, and it's fun in crossover, but if you're just werewolf and looking for &quot;faerie guest-stars&quot; then it's a wash.</div> </div> </div> </div>The one player who is big on Changeling included various things in his backgrounds that are Changeling specific. Basically, there are people in his family who are Kinain. So while I do not feel bound to every detail in Changeling canon, I want it to be recognizable. I normally would not go into much detail for this, but I'm indulging him. It's a big part of what makes the game fun for him.<br /> <br /> So I'm a softie. Sue me. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Of course, I'm not doing the things with it he expected. But that makes it fun for him too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Werewolf sources pose Fae as hazardous tricksters and semi-elemental spirits, scions of the Wyld who are rapidly fading away from the onslaught of mankind, but who are still not to be trifled with. If you give the pack a 9 year-old kid who insists he's really a six-foot-tall blue dude but he can't show them... it doesn't work well. </div> </div> </div>Yes, this is the big trouble with Changeling. It's part Narnia, part Gormenghast, part Neverwhere, and part folklore. It's like 80% there to be a great comprehensive sandbox setting, but White Wolf didn't really make it coherent. It's like a rough draft that showed promise, but needed several more revisions and a good editor.<br /> <br /> I find the easiest way to make it work for me is increase the number and importance of sentient Chimera, and establish Changelings as unique to bridge the gap between mortal and the Dreaming, mainly because without mortal blood to rejuvenate the race, the Dreaming is slowly dying.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Forget Changeling, and think &quot;Fae&quot;. </div> </div> </div>I have twenty-one volumes of Time-Life Book's Enchanted World series. Between that and Mike Mignola's Hellboy, I know how I want to portray the Fae.<br /> <br /> It's just figuring out the details of interaction between Fae and Garou I've been struggling with. But I've gotten some good feedback here.<br /> <br /> Thanks for your comments.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T15:05:50-07:00","id":611395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/603273-changeling-involvement-with-garou-that-makes-sense?p=611392#post611392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have twenty-one volumes of Time-Life Book's Enchanted World series.</div> </div> </div> </div>I shall just sit here, scowling in a silent jealous rage. With my five. Two of which are badly water-damaged. Growl.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/612-the-cat-came-back","name":"The Cat Came Back","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar612_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"243"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}